WEBVTT

NOTE Cue timings are estimated from sentence length and pauses in the audio.

1
00:00:00.300 --> 00:00:04.590
Welcome to the Concilium Security Risk Brief for Saturday, November fourteenth.

2
00:00:04.590 --> 00:00:13.517
Five minutes of security coverage from the last twenty four hours, to increase your situational awareness without decreasing your productivity.

3
00:00:13.517 --> 00:00:14.388
Here's what matters today.

4
00:00:14.388 --> 00:00:29.612
Today: a nationwide flight ground stop in the United States, the U.S. military disputes Iran's claim about a radar in Bahrain, a hostage release and a motorcycle bomb in Colombia, a car bomb in Moscow, and attacks on health workers slowing Congo's Ebola response.

5
00:00:29.612 --> 00:00:34.095
We start with air travel in the United States.

6
00:00:34.095 --> 00:00:45.155
Australia's Smartraveller, Canada's travel advice service and Britain's Foreign Office all updated their U.S. advice after the Federal Aviation Administration issued a nationwide ground stop for all U.S. airports yesterday.

7
00:00:45.155 --> 00:00:54.759
The Express Tribune reports the F A A cited extraordinary circumstances, with the disruption linked to a telecommunications failure affecting air traffic control centers.

8
00:00:54.759 --> 00:01:05.438
Smartraveller and Canada say the ground stop has since been lifted, but delays and cancellations continue, and both advise checking with your airline.

9
00:01:05.438 --> 00:01:06.500
Next, Iran and Bahrain.

10
00:01:06.500 --> 00:01:10.341
In an update on Iran's claim that it targeted a U.S. early warning radar in Bahrain, U.S.

11
00:01:10.341 --> 00:01:21.276
Central Command says the Revolutionary Guards launched two one way attack drones toward Bahrain, both were shot down by U.S. forces, and there were no injuries or damage.

12
00:01:21.276 --> 00:01:30.665
Separately, Reuters reports, citing sources, that President Trump has told advisers he may hold off on attacks on Iran barring new provocations.

13
00:01:30.665 --> 00:01:31.600
Turning to Colombia.

14
00:01:31.600 --> 00:01:42.210
The International Committee of the Red Cross says that on Thursday, November twelfth, it helped secure the release of two people held captive by the E L N's Eastern War Front in Arauca.

15
00:01:42.210 --> 00:01:52.548
That same night in Cali, a motorcycle bomb exploded near the Carabineros police school in the Siloé area as a police patrol passed, according to Revista Semana and local broadcaster Canal T R O.

16
00:01:52.548 --> 00:01:57.121
No official casualty figures were reported in those accounts.

17
00:01:57.121 --> 00:02:08.039
In Russia, A F P reports a car bomb in Moscow's Chertanovo district seriously injured Sergei Zavorotny, a former adviser to Ukraine's pro Russian ex prime minister Mykola Azarov.

18
00:02:08.039 --> 00:02:18.981
The Moscow Times reports Russia's Investigative Committee confirmed he was hospitalized in serious condition, and the state news agency TASS says investigators opened an attempted murder case.

19
00:02:18.981 --> 00:02:21.539
And in the Democratic Republic of the Congo.

20
00:02:21.539 --> 00:02:33.773
Reuters reports Africa's top public health agency says attacks on health workers and facilities are increasingly hindering efforts to contain the Ebola outbreak in the east, which has killed more than fifty four hundred people.

21
00:02:33.773 --> 00:02:41.690
The U.N. humanitarian office's senior Ebola coordinator says the response has made real progress, but significant risks persist.

22
00:02:41.690 --> 00:02:43.829
Now a few quick notes by region.

23
00:02:43.829 --> 00:02:54.353
In the Middle East, an update on Yemen: the Institute for the Study of War says government aligned forces halted the Houthi offensive in southeastern Lahij province and recaptured territory.

24
00:02:54.353 --> 00:03:01.300
And the Long War Journal reports Iran's Baluch insurgency has expanded with a new faction merger.

25
00:03:01.300 --> 00:03:06.150
In Europe, Reuters reports Russian strikes killed one person in Zaporizhzhia and two in Odesa.

26
00:03:06.150 --> 00:03:11.018
Reuters also reports U.S.

27
00:03:11.018 --> 00:03:19.082
Air Force personnel at R A F Lakenheath in Britain responded to suspected unauthorized drone activity, with no personnel, aircraft or infrastructure affected, a spokesperson said.

28
00:03:19.082 --> 00:03:21.577
In the Americas, the U.S.

29
00:03:21.577 --> 00:03:31.165
Treasury's OFAC sanctioned the Guatemala based Los Mendoza and Los Huistas drug trafficking organizations for supporting the Sinaloa Cartel and the Jalisco New Generation Cartel.

30
00:03:31.165 --> 00:03:40.075
The U.N. humanitarian office says violence in Croix des Bouquets, near Port au Prince, Haiti, has displaced around two thousand people since mid October.

31
00:03:40.075 --> 00:03:47.275
InSight Crime reports a Tren de Aragua faction allegedly planned a car bomb attack outside a courthouse in Arica, Chile.

32
00:03:47.275 --> 00:03:48.068
And the U.S.

33
00:03:48.068 --> 00:03:58.570
Embassy in Mexico encourages U.S. citizens in western coastal states, including Baja California, Sinaloa and Jalisco, to prepare for potential impacts of El Niño.

34
00:03:58.570 --> 00:04:05.786
And in cyber, Microsoft says an active phishing campaign is impersonating Microsoft 365 service health notices to exploit this week's service disruption.

35
00:04:05.786 --> 00:04:15.155
Microsoft also details a campaign abusing the ScreenConnect remote support tool to target managed service providers.

36
00:04:15.155 --> 00:04:21.744
The Record reports chipmaker T S M C says employee data was stolen after a cloud service provider was breached.

37
00:04:21.744 --> 00:04:23.146
That's today's brief.

38
00:04:23.146 --> 00:04:31.296
These security developments come from government travel advisories and trusted analysts, curated by the Concilium Security Risk Management Team.

39
00:04:31.296 --> 00:04:39.404
The brief summarizes public reporting and isn't a substitute for your own risk assessment, so check the original source before making travel decisions.

40
00:04:39.404 --> 00:04:41.553
This brief is digitally narrated.

41
00:04:41.553 --> 00:04:42.494
Questions?

42
00:04:42.494 --> 00:04:45.951
Reach Concilium at info at concilium dot U.S.

43
00:04:45.951 --> 00:04:48.028
Thanks for listening, and stay safe.
